  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "4hsY/+bCVoiYPVUqzVo469BLFAo=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:19:27.084Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The specification's own README is careful about what its green run means. The Phase-1 model is bounded, and the limits are enumerated: only **2 reactors** (not N), only **1 document** (multi-document scenarios untested), at most **3 operations per reactor**, and a high level of abstraction that omits implementation detail. It explicitly does **not** model:\n\n- network failures or partitions,\n- crash recovery,\n- authentication and authorization,\n- cryptographic signatures,\n- performance characteristics.\n\nThe authors' interpretation is worth quoting in spirit: the spec proves correctness for the bounded case, which gives high confidence but **is not a proof for unbounded systems** \u2014 real-world edge cases with many reactors, documents and operations may still exist.\n\nTwo further phases are named and not implemented: Phase 2 (2 reactors, 2 documents, 5 operations, expected 10\u201330 minutes) and Phase 3 (3 reactors if tractable, network partitions, 1\u20132 hours). Anyone citing \"the sync protocol is formally verified\" should say which phase they mean.\n\nThe mapping table is the useful bridge for readers of the code: `streams` is `IOperationStore` per document/scope/branch, `channels.inbox` is a `SyncOperation` in `ExecutionPending`, `channels.outbox` one in `TransportPending`, `cursors` is `ISyncCursorStorage`, and `PerformReshuffle` is `reshuffleByTimestamp()`.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/reactor/specs/tla/README.md` \u2014 Limitations; Future Phases; Mapping to Implementation\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:19:27.084Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:19:27.084Z"
    }
  },
  {
    "index": 4,
